  "ecological_interpretation": "Larger Palmer Adelie breeding groups show higher reproductive output per pair relative to a frozen proportional-productivity null, providing independent evidence of positive group-size dependence. However, only four durable-extinction events have matched pre-extinction chick data and their reproductive-success deficit is non-confirmatory. Combined with the separate size-conditioned extinction null, group-size biology is present but a causal pathway from reduced group size to durable local extinction is not established.",
  "claim_boundary": [
    "Do not use small-first extinction ordering itself as evidence for an Allee effect or skua mechanism.",
    "Do not claim that low chick productivity caused the observed durable extinctions.",
    "The positive group-size productivity gradient is consistent with social facilitation, size-dependent protection, or correlated habitat quality; it does not distinguish among them.",
    "The adult-census size predictor is independent enough from the chick-dataset denominator to avoid treating a shared-denominator association as the primary evidence."
  ]
